// 1985. Iris is twenty-four: the kitchen, one word from her father, and the last bus north.

== kitchen_1985                                  # talk · picture kitchen_1985
The scholarship letter has been on the fridge for a month. The last bus north leaves at 22:40. Her case has been packed since Sunday.
Dad has been ill since the spring. He doesn't look up.   # pause 0.3
DAD: Go.
- (ask)
* Who'll run the shop?
  DAD: I ran it before you could walk. I'll run it after you've gone.
  -> ask
* You're not well.
  DAD: I'm not dead. Go.
  -> ask
* { carried has play } You could still play, Dad.        # known play
  DAD: Who'd listen?
  The same two words. You were eight, behind the piano. He doesn't know you heard them.
  -> ask
* { carried has gave } You gave yours up.                # known gave
  He looks up for the first time.
  DAD: And look what I got for it.
  He means her. He means it.
  -> ask
* Pick up the case.
  DAD: Go on. Go.
  22:31. The bus stop is four minutes away.
  -> fork_1985

